igoplus\\nolimits_{\\varphi \\in \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(V, U)} \\mathcal{O}(V)\n$$", "source_byte_span": {"end": 1282, "start": 1112}, "source_hash": "sha256:41c9d2be965827322e02f4be54ad8a829a6c3c35fb9db1f63eca240f18142807"}], "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03FA", "placeholders": {"MATHSEG_0001": "$$\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{\\varphi' \\in \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(V, U')} \\mathcal{O}(V)\n\\quad\\text{", "MATHSEG_0002": "}\\quad\n\\bigoplus\\nolimits_{\\varphi \\in \\Mor_\\mathcal{C}(V, U)} \\mathcal{O}(V)\n$$", "MATH_0001": "$j : \\mathcal{C}/U \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$j' : \\mathcal{C}/U' \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$j_!$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\Hom_\\mathcal{O}(j_!\\mathcal{O}_U, \\mathcal{F})\n=\n\\Hom_{\\mathcal{O}_U}(\\mathcal{O}_U, \\mathcal{F}|_U)\n=\n\\mathcal{F}(U)\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$j'_!\\mathcal{O}_{U'}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{F} \\mapsto \\mathcal{F}(U')$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0010": "$$\nj'_!\\mathcal{O}_{U'} \\longrightarrow j_!\\mathcal{O}_U\n$$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}(U')$", "MATH_0012": "$V$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{O}(V)$", "MATH_0015": "$\\varphi'$", "MATH_0016": "$\\varphi = a \\circ \\varphi'$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{O}(V)$", "MATH_0018": "$a$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sites-modules-section-localize}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-lemma-yoneda}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{homology-lemma-characterize-injectives}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{sites-modules-lemma-extension-by-zero}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 2, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:728cf36557eb6ac31004bca5091368228d7b9161d477b1ecfa829a18d1013161", "source_math_skeleton_hash": "sha256:56aa15399702254fe059025fde28572d13d46e0e07421a0b0e1e67e757b00a96", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5413482cafa46483a27374118e968a16d84671c3323cabfd2178de5967ecf045", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and\n<MATH_0002> be the localization morphisms\n(Modules on Sites, Section <REF_0001>).\nSince <MATH_0003> is a left adjoint to restriction we see that\nfor any sheaf <MATH_0004> of <MATH_0005>-modules\n<MATH_0006>\nSimilarly, the sheaf <MATH_0007> represents the\nfunctor <MATH_0008>.\nMoreover below we describe a canonical map of <MATH_0009>-modules\n<MATH_0010>\nwhich corresponds to the restriction mapping\n<MATH_0011> via Yoneda's lemma\n(Categories, Lemma <REF_0002>).\nIt suffices to prove the displayed map of modules is injective, see\nHomology, Lemma <REF_0003>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nTo construct our map it suffices to construct a map between the\npresheaves which assign to an object <MATH_0012> of <MATH_0013> the\n<MATH_0014>-module\n<MATHSEG_0001>and<MATHSEG_0002>\nsee Modules on Sites, Lemma <REF_0004>.\nWe take the map which maps the summand corresponding to <MATH_0015>\nto the summand corresponding to <MATH_0016>\nby the identity map on <MATH_0017>. As <MATH_0018> is a monomorphism,\nthis map is injective. As sheafification is exact, the result\nfollows.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:57934d60498ba6631657fc186ea229acc7b0dd6fca9f15cd21a662409591f159", "unit_id": "tag:093X:proof"}
